 </costs>
 </selectionEntry>
 <selectionEntry id="91c0637f-b744-56f7-8086-b19832873ec4" name="15th Legion - Illusion Arcana" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
 <rules><rule id="11f35722-0c1a-5685-8d55-8601b9bd0900" name="15th Legion - Illusion Arcana" hidden="false"><description>Once per battle in your Command Phase, until your next Command Phase enemies suffer −1 BS targeting friendly ships.</description></rule></rules><categoryLinks>
 <categoryLink id="fbeea4d2-5a42-5cab-a631-182f3f5ed27e" name="Rules" hidden="false" targetId="52616092-abd8-519e-a6fb-94b622114fa5" primary="true" /></categoryLinks>
 <costs><cost name="pts" typeId="570b7f63-4fc7-515c-9c96-5b5c25501f85" value="0.0" /></costs></selectionEntry>
 </selectionEntries>
 <sharedSelectionEntries />
<sharedSelectionEntryGroups /><sharedRules><rule id="7e63fc7f-8d9a-5fc3-8889-f4f2b01917f2" name="15th Legion - Illusion Arcana" hidden="false"><description>Once per battle in your Command Phase, until your next Command Phase enemies suffer −1 BS targeting friendly ships.</description></rule><rule id="9a13e0ea-a9e3-5a9e-88e5-40687b037c2f" name="1st Legion - The First Legion" hidden="false"><description /></rule><rule id="06f5379c-3756-598c-a902-667b47d42dc5" name="Ship Construction" hidden="false"><description>Ships are bought as a bare chassis and armed hardpoint by hardpoint. Every weapon and Defence Battery on a mount is paid for separately; Hangar Bay slots are built-in hull capacity and cost 0 pts. Each mount group shows its capacity — Defence Mounts 0/8, for instance — and you choose how many of that mount to fill. A hull filled with its standard armament costs exactly its rulebook price. There is no separate upgrade-spend ceiling: mount count and facing are the limits.</description></rule><rule id="052c1e73-b54e-53d4-b434-5da84da672dc" name="Fleet Commanders" hidden="false"><description>Every fleet has exactly one commander, the highest rank present, riding the Flagship and lost if that ship is destroyed, captured or wrecked. Orders of each type per battle round: Fleet Captain 1, Named Character 2, Primarch 3 — unless that commander's own entry states otherwise. Ranks never combine, and no ship, ability or upgrade adds to the allowance: where a datasheet grants a different number, that number replaces the rank's rather than adding to it. Each rank carries its own command ability: Ship’s Master, Practised Command, or The Fleet Obeys.</description></rule><rule id="5fe4558c-3ed7-5c03-9156-785122c60958" name="The Battle Round" hidden="false"><description>1. Muster — flip Reload tokens and remove any reaching 0, refresh the fleet's Fleet Order allowance, declare Reactor Overloads. In the first battle round roll off for Initiative; in every later round it passes to whoever finished the previous round. The holder moves, shoots and rams first for the whole round. 2. Movement — alternate one ship each, then one aircraft squadron each. 3. Shooting — alternate one ship or squadron each. 4. Ramming &amp; Boarding — alternate one ship each. 5. End of round — resolve dogfights, then Critical Damage. A game lasts six rounds, and every duration runs to the end of the battle round unless it names something else.</description></rule><rule id="e0a7883b-40a7-569a-b79e-507fd78b6237" name="Movement" hidden="false"><description>A ship moves at least half its Speed and never more than 12″ (All Ahead Full excepted). It may make one turn per battle round, up to its Turn value, taken either at the start or at the end of its move — no straight run is required before turning. Ships may never overlap unless a Ram is declared; accidental contact stops the moving ship 1″ short.</description></rule><rule id="4459dfc4-831f-5f8a-9159-1f7a7fa4964e" name="Shooting" hidden="false"><description>A ship fires everything that bears at one enemy ship each round — it never divides its fire, though a squadron may. Roll a D6 per shot, hitting on 7 − BS. A natural 1 always misses and no modifier lowers the roll below 2+. Modifiers: target is an Destroyer or Frigate that moved its full Speed −1; target is a wreck +1. A ship that held station under Burn Retros fires its Port and Starboard broadsides at +1 BS.</description></rule><rule id="2b404038-c84e-5906-9383-5cc501cc8eb2" name="Void Shields" hidden="false"><description>While Void Shield Rating is above 0 the shields are Armour Value 12 and every hit strikes them rather than the hull. Roll 1D6 + Strength against AV 12; equal or better collapses one layer and does nothing else — no Hull Points, no Damage Table. There is no save. At VS 0 the shields collapse permanently, with no restoration or repair, and AP applies in full. Torpedo Tubes, Vortex Torpedoes, Melta Mines and the Abyss's Warp Lance Batteries bypass shields entirely. Nothing else does.</description></rule><rule id="73a419bf-84a7-5c4c-b504-9a40c3623cc6" name="Penetration" hidden="false"><description>For each hit past the shields, roll 1D6 + Strength against the Armour Value of the facing struck. Equal = Glancing Hit: 1 Hull Point, no damage roll. Greater = Penetrating Hit: 1 Hull Point and a roll on the Damage Table. No Armour Value may exceed 14 by any means.</description></rule><rule id="35499ed1-0a27-5b44-9c4e-1943353dc1f1" name="Point-Blank Broadsides" hidden="false"><description>At 6″ or less, Port, Starboard and Dorsal weapons improve their AP by one step — a Macrobattery to AP 2, a Heavy Macrobattery to AP 1. A weapon whose printed AP is already 1 gains Armourbane instead. Never both, and Prow weapons get neither.</description></rule><rule id="9a470b39-a69b-583b-998f-e6a4b08ef05d" name="Stern Strike" hidden="false"><description>When a Strength 9+ weapon rolls a natural 6 on its penetration die against a target's Stern and beats the Stern AV, the hit also inflicts Engines Crippled at once. With Armourbane at least one of the two dice must show a 6. It does not stack with an Engines Crippled already rolled, and while shields hold the hit must bring them down first.</description></rule><rule id="18dd061c-4d5f-5518-a34c-05895bf78a67" name="Ship Damage Table" hidden="false"><description>Roll a D6 when a Penetrating Hit is scored. Modifiers: AP 2 +1 • AP 1 +2 • Destroyer +3 in place of any AP modifier, +2 against a Gloriana, the Abyss or the Phalanx • Ramming +1 • Battleship target −1. A modified 7+ counts as Reactor Struck; below 1 counts as 1, and a 1 does nothing.
1 HELD • Immediate: none. • Ongoing: none.
2 BLAZE • Immediate: 1 Critical Damage. • Ongoing: the ship loses 1 Crew at the end of each battle round for each Critical Damage it carries. • Repair: Damage Control clears the whole stack at once.
3 HULL BREACH • Immediate: 1 Critical Damage. • Ongoing and repair: as Blaze.
4 MAGAZINE EXPLOSION • Immediate: 1 Hull Point, 2 if the ship mounts Triple Lance Turrets, plus 1 Critical Damage, and one random Port, Starboard or Dorsal weapon system destroyed. • Ongoing: the destroyed system cannot fire. • Repair: Damage Control may repair one destroyed system. • Note: Reinforced Magazine Compartments reduces the Damage Control suffered by 1, to a minimum of 0.
5 ENGINES CRIPPLED • Immediate: immobile, and Snap Shots only. • Ongoing: no Firing at anchor bonus, and −1 on Evade. It may still be issued Fleet Orders. A second result leaves the ship Adrift — 2D6″ straight ahead, no turning. • Repair: Damage Control clears it, Adrift becoming Engines Crippled.
6 REACTOR STRUCK • Immediate: a Line Ship suffers a Catastrophic Explosion at once; a Capital Ship takes D3 Hull Points then rolls a D6, detonating on a 6; a Gloriana or larger takes D3 and rolls 2D6, detonating if either die shows a 6. • Ongoing: none. • Repair: none.</description></rule><rule id="d6c3b6b4-29dc-5a0c-9e0b-811e2b498f48" name="Destruction" hidden="false"><description>At 0 Hull Points roll a D6 once: on a 6 the ship is torn apart in a Catastrophic Explosion and every ship within the blast radius suffers one hit against its nearest facing — Str 8 AP 3 from a Line Ship, Str 9 AP 2 from a Capital Ship or Void Fortress. On any other result it becomes a wreck. Blast radius: Destroyer, Frigate or Assault Barge 3″ · Cruiser D6″ · Grand Cruiser or Battle Barge D6+3″ · Battleship or Gloriana 2D6″ · Abyss 3D6″.</description></rule><rule id="4907c98c-1473-5b29-af0f-36b5df5ca2dd" name="Ramming" hidden="false"><description>Free, needing no Fleet Order, against one enemy within 6″ of the rammer's prow. Roll a D6, −1 if the rammer mounts a prow Nova Cannon bought as an upgrade; the ram connects if it equals or beats the distance in inches. The target may Evade on 5+. On impact the target suffers one hit at Strength = the rammer's Prow AV, ignoring Void Shields, penetrating on 1D6 + Str with no Armourbane; a hit that glances or penetrates inflicts D6 Hull Points and a penetrating hit rolls on the Damage Table at +1. The rammer loses D3 Hull Points. Survivors remain Locked.</description></rule><rule id="64866eee-7681-560d-a0c2-adaa5cdd231e" name="Fleet Orders" hidden="false"><description>Only the Flagship issues orders, within 24″ Command range, and no order needs a test. Each battle round the fleet may issue orders of each of the three types up to its commander's rank: Fleet Captain 1, Named Character 2, Primarch 3. No ship takes two orders of the same type in a round, ranks never combine, and nothing adds to the allowance. Unspent orders do not carry over.
DAMAGE CONTROL (Command) • Issued: in the ship's activation. • Target: one friendly ship in range. • Effect: roll a D6, Legion fleets re-rolling; on 4+ choose one — remove every Critical Damage, repair one destroyed weapon system, or clear Engines Crippled. • Duration: immediate. • Restriction: the ship fires only Snap Shots this round.
FOCUS FIRE (Command) • Issued: as the ship fires. • Target: one friendly ship, against one enemy ship. • Effect: +1 BS. • Duration: this round. • Restriction: shares the single +1 pool with the anchor bonus and accuracy auras.
BRACE FOR IMPACT (Command, Reaction) • Issued: the moment this ship is attacked. • Effect: halve all Hull Point loss, rounding up. • Duration: to the end of the round. • Restriction: the ship fires only Snap Shots until then.
ALL AHEAD FULL (Movement) • Issued: as the ship moves. • Effect: move +D6″, beyond the 12″ ceiling. • Restriction: may fire only Defence Batteries.
BURN RETROS (Movement) • Issued: as the ship moves. • Effect: move less than half Speed or not at all; a ship holding station (1″ or less) may pivot freely and fires its broadsides at +1 BS. • Restriction: −1 on Evade rolls.
EVADE (Movement, Reaction) • Issued: when this ship is shot at or rammed, before any dice are rolled. • Effect: on 5+ the whole attack misses, or the ram fails and the rammer is moved 1″ past. • Modifiers: +1 Destroyer or Frigate; −1 held station; −1 Crippled, Adrift or Engines Crippled; −1 mounting no standard Macrobatteries; never worse than −2. • Restriction: once per battle round; wrecks and Speed 0 installations never Evade.
RELOAD ORDNANCE (Shooting) • Issued: as the ship fires. • Target: one weapon system on a friendly ship. • Effect: remove one Reload token. • Restriction: a system bearing no token cannot be chosen.
RETURN FIRE (Shooting, Reaction) • Issued: when this ship is attacked and survives. • Effect: fire back at −1 to hit with every weapon that bears on the attacker. • Restriction: not systems already fired this round, nor one-shot or reloading weapons.
OVERWATCH (Shooting, Reaction) • Issued: when a boarding craft or drop pod runs at this ship. • Effect: snap-fire Defence Batteries at that craft; destroyed on 5+. • Restriction: Defence Batteries only.</description></rule><rule id="4fb1294d-5452-561e-b81b-231333c564e6" name="Orders Need No Test" hidden="false"><description>No Fleet Order needs a test — the word is given and obeyed. There is no Morale, no Leadership and no test of a crew's nerve anywhere in the game; a damaged ship is measured by the Crippled and Depleted penalties alone. Command ranks instead carry their own abilities: Ship's Master, Practised Command, and the Primarch's own.</description></rule><rule id="c9cc6eb7-507e-5eb4-b359-f78f41cb7069" name="Reactions" hidden="false"><description>Brace for Impact, Return Fire and Overwatch are Fleet Orders with a trigger, issued the moment a friendly ship is attacked or targeted, whether or not that ship has already acted. They count against the round's allowance however many ships are under fire — an order spent defending is one you no longer have for your own turn.</description></rule><rule id="4839d2e2-9187-56b0-aa1f-a11a61a6afed" name="Evade" hidden="false"><description>A Movement order, declared when the ship is shot at or rammed and before any dice are rolled. Roll a D6: on a 5+ the whole attack misses, or the ram fails and the rammer is moved 1″ past its intended victim. Modifiers: +1 Destroyer or Frigate · −1 held station · −1 Crippled, Adrift or Engines Crippled · −1 mounting no standard Macrobatteries. Never worse than −2. Once per battle round; wrecks and Speed 0 installations never Evade.</description></rule><rule id="da89907f-6564-5b60-b959-4fc0b4bf8cc4" name="Boarding Actions" hidden="false"><description>Crew are the hit points of boarding, and an action begins and ends in one Ramming &amp; Boarding step. Declare the Crew committed and the delivery method, then deduct them; a ship always keeps 1 aboard. Every fighter rolls his own D6 with his own bonus, and bonuses never combine into one roll. Starting with the boarders, players alternate nominating duels: the higher total fells its opponent, and ties re-roll until one is higher. Fight on until one side reaches 0 Crew or the boarders withdraw. Defenders reduced to 0 lose the ship — Capture or Scuttle. Modifiers to every die on that side: +1 boarders in the first round if delivered by craft, pod or teleport (never a Hull Assault) · +1 boarders if the enemy ship is Crippled · +1 boarders if it is Engines Crippled · −1 defenders if the ship carries any Critical Damage.</description></rule><rule id="abe65c61-9fb9-5465-a954-436f40621259" name="Hit-and-Run" hidden="false"><description>Instead of a full boarding, commit 1 Crew — so never a Dreadnought, which is two. Roll D6 plus the raider's own bonus. On 4+ choose one: destroy one weapon system or Hangar Bay; inflict 1 Critical Damage; cripple the enginarium (Engines Crippled); or sabotage the shields, reducing VS Rating by D3, or D6 against a Capital Ship, permanently. The raider returns. On a failure the raider is lost.</description></rule><rule id="e1900047-8897-5744-a23a-57155c94cbe4" name="Attrition" hidden="false"><description>There is no Morale. Ships do not flee and take no tests — they fight until wrecked, taken, or the battle ends, and they fight worse as they break down. Crippled and Depleted stack, so a ship can fire at −2. Broken Fleet: once three quarters of a fleet's starting points are lost it loses the battle at once. Count a lost ship at full cost, upgrades and any Fleet Commander aboard included; aircraft never count.</description></rule><rule id="0abc8585-49ef-549f-920e-6db6fb5bcc03" name="Fleet Construction" hidden="false"><description>Capital Ship allowance is generated by Line Ships: for every 4 individual Line Ships in the fleet you may include 1 Capital Ship. 0–3 Line Ships permit no Capital Ship; 4–7 permit 1; 8–11 permit 2; 12–15 permit 3, and so on — maximum Capital Ships = Line Ships ÷ 4, rounded down. Individual vessels count, not roster entries: a squadron of four Destroyers is four Line Ships. Line Ships are the Destroyer, Frigate, Light Cruiser, Assault Barge and Cruiser. Capital Ships are the Grand Cruiser, Battle Barge, Battleship, Emperor Battleship, Gloriana and Abyss, and the Phalanx above them. No single ship may exceed 50% of the fleet's points, upgrades included. Destroyers and Frigates have the Squadron keyword: each is taken singly, and up to 3 may be grouped into one squadron. Minimum game size: Gloriana 2,000; Abyss and Phalanx 3,000.</description></rule><rule id="c0f3c086-3385-50ad-b10e-97397d4b4af7" name="Veteran Crews &amp; Commanders" hidden="false"><description>Any ship may take a Veteran Crew once: +1 Ballistic Skill for the battle, 60 pts for a Line Ship and 150 pts for a Capital Ship. No ship exceeds BS 5, and a ship takes at most one +1 BS from position or command — Firing at anchor, Focus Fire and accuracy auras never stack with each other. A Veteran Crew's +1 is a paid upgrade and stacks on top. Every fleet has exactly one commander, the highest rank present, riding the Flagship and lost if that ship is destroyed, captured or wrecked. Each rank carries its own command ability: Ship’s Master, Practised Command, or The Fleet Obeys.</description></rule><rule id="ae80c180-30f0-5dbd-929f-546c45d2c187" name="Keyword: Armourbane" hidden="false"><description>Roll 2D6 + Strength to penetrate instead of 1D6, at 6″ or less, against shields or hull alike. Torpedo Tubes and the Starhawk's plasma bombs carry it outright; a broadside or dorsal weapon of printed AP 1 gains it inside 6″ in place of the AP step it cannot take. Macrobatteries never gain it, and neither do rams — the Conqueror's Ursus Claws excepted. Destroyer weapons never roll to penetrate, so it does nothing for them.</description></rule><rule id="787149b5-a010-5aaf-82c2-99957a734fe5" name="Keyword: Destroyer (D)" hidden="false"><description>Any weapon of AP D. Strength never exceeds 12. It penetrates automatically — no roll, whatever the Armour Value — and can never merely glance. Every Damage Table roll it causes is made at +3 in place of any AP modifier, or +2 against a Gloriana, the Abyss or the Phalanx. It is always at least Devastating (3). It does not pass Void Shields: while they hold it beats AV 12 automatically and collapses 3 layers, and does nothing else. The Destroyer hull class and the Destroyer (D) weapon keyword are unrelated. A Destroyer fires ordinary weapons at their printed AP; Destroyer (D) weapons are the Nova Cannon and the Vortex Torpedo, which are AP D and are carried only by the Battleship and above.</description></rule><rule id="420c18d1-5fc3-59cc-a017-3e3e1fe4d1d1" name="Keyword: Devastating (X)" hidden="false"><description>Each unsaved hit costs the target X Hull Points instead of 1, whether it glances or penetrates. A penetrating Devastating hit still rolls once on the Damage Table, keeping its AP modifier. Against active shields a Devastating hit still costs only 1 Void Shield Rating, however large its X.</description></rule><rule id="e827d0e3-4e63-51e2-ac71-e7d506e552d0" name="Keyword: Gets Hot" hidden="false"><description>After a Lance Turret or Twin Lance Turret has resolved its attacks, roll a D6. On a 1 the firing ship suffers 1 Hull Point. Each mount rolls separately. Self-inflicted rolls have no attacker or facing: the owning player makes any choices, from any facing, but must choose a functioning system.</description></rule><rule id="c7d308c3-83b4-52c2-84c8-ec4fe51d3699" name="Keyword: One Shot" hidden="false"><description>Fired once per battle, then spent. It takes no Reload tokens.</description></rule><rule id="381e2173-7dec-5c15-962a-0fcb24aaaf04" name="Keyword: Reload (X)" hidden="false"><description>After firing, place X Reload tokens on the mount. Flip the token at the end of each battle round — 2 becomes 1 — and remove it when it would reach 0. The mount cannot fire while it bears a token, so Reload (1) speaks every round and Reload (2) every second. The Reload Ordnance order removes one counter early.</description></rule><rule id="bf93286c-a63d-50ac-843d-dd0a77be7a26" name="Keyword: Skyfire" hidden="false"><description>Fires at full Ballistic Skill against aircraft.</description></rule><rule id="d91d6eb7-04b1-5929-ba24-425f047207f1" name="Keyword: Twin-Linked" hidden="false"><description>Re-roll failed To Hit rolls.</description></rule><rule id="1c2dfe88-314a-531e-8727-244b0db89e36" name="Keyword: Volatile" hidden="false"><description>An unmodified 1 To Hit resolves the attack against the firing ship instead, at the full profile — against the facing the launcher is mounted in. The launcher is spent either way.</description></rule><rule id="0a63e5be-cf44-50d0-aa0d-12ffebcf8d3e" name="Keyword: Critical Damage" hidden="false"><description>Fires, breaches and burning phosphex — one rule for all of them. A ship may carry up to 3 Critical Damage, marked with a single token. At the end of each battle round it loses 1 Crew for each Critical Damage it carries, always, with no roll. A successful Damage Control order clears the whole stack at once.</description></rule><rule id="d5536739-0eba-5de2-af09-59aad2681055" name="Mounts &amp; Arcs" hidden="false"><description>Prow — the forward 90° arc. Port / Starboard — that side's 90° arc; these are the broadsides. Dorsal — every arc but the Stern; counts as a broadside for Point-Blank Broadsides, but gains no Firing at anchor bonus. All-round — every arc. Straight ahead — Torpedo Tubes only: a line drawn directly forward from the prow, and only a ship that line crosses may be targeted. The facing struck is whichever of the target's arcs the firer sits in. Broadsides are per side: each line of a datasheet is its own weapon system in that facing.</description></rule><rule id="8ab9ff2f-486b-5fea-9139-8441fc608790" name="State: Adrift" hidden="false"><description>A second Engines Crippled. The ship moves 2D6″ straight ahead when it would move, cannot turn, and fires Snap Shots only.</description></rule><rule id="f4f251f8-a583-54d9-912e-ed1dd287e45d" name="State: Crippled" hidden="false"><description>Below half starting Hull Points: −1 BS and half Speed.</description></rule><rule id="7bc7d2ad-3f5d-58eb-beea-ea90d408e2fb" name="State: Depleted" hidden="false"><description>At half starting Crew or less: −1 BS. Stacks with Crippled.</description></rule><rule id="e60b607b-7d6f-5a7f-bee0-c7c431a28793" name="State: Engaged" hidden="false"><description>Two aircraft squadrons within 1″. Neither may act against ships, and no ship may fire on either — Defence Batteries, Interceptor and Overwatch included. Resolved at the end of the battle round.</description></rule><rule id="1e74af5e-5506-5508-9276-280598ef531a" name="State: Engines Crippled" hidden="false"><description>Immobile and Snap Shots only until repaired. It may still be issued Fleet Orders. It gains no Firing at anchor bonus for standing still, though it still suffers −1 on Evade.</description></rule><rule id="d12a5e32-4c5f-5e82-ab0b-ec3ad5365e7a" name="State: Held station" hidden="false"><description>Moved 1″ or less under Burn Retros. Broadsides fire at +1 BS; −1 on Evade. A ship holding station may pivot freely on the spot.</description></rule><rule id="18eb31b2-2342-5aba-a4ad-605ecac98f63" name="State: Locked" hidden="false"><description>Two ships joined by a ram. Neither may move; the rammer may not fire on its victim, who fires back at −1 BS against the rammer's Prow. Both fire at other enemies normally. Break Away on 5+, when the ship would move, once each per battle round: the rammer disengages 1″ away, a defender tears free 1″ away and suffers D3 Hull Points.</description></rule><rule id="5ab8c30c-b90d-5cf0-ac1f-d7e926585965" name="State: Snap Shots" hidden="false"><description>Firing at BS 1 — hits only on a 6.</description></rule><rule id="061c63e0-a768-52cb-a5a2-9f0dbf7d33d5" name="State: Wreck" hidden="false"><description>0 Hull Points without exploding. It becomes obscuring terrain: impassable, blocks line of sight, and no straight-line weapon may fire across it. It never moves, never drifts and never Evades, and having no Crew it cannot be boarded or captured.</description></rule><rule id="e820b068-ef9b-59af-8765-57f93e10aeef" name="Keyword: Turning" hidden="false"><description>Turning is universal: any ship may turn at the start or the end of its move.</description></rule><rule id="21af72dc-2d49-53e9-8832-5f2b98bf61f1" name="Keyword: Interceptor" hidden="false"><description>A Defence Battery may fire the moment an enemy squadron comes within 12″ as the enemy moves, before it attacks — but then does nothing else that battle round, Overwatch included.</description></rule><rule id="4a00efcb-0a3d-51c9-8fe4-ee27f9309a63" name="Keyword: Breachers" hidden="false"><description>+1 to all Boarding combat rolls, and enemy dice fighting them suffer −1. The −1 of a Dreadnought, or of an Astartes Breacher defending his own ship, falls on the one enemy die paired against him.</description></rule><rule id="f33aea75-9729-5297-976a-cf59e4483a4a" name="Keyword: Intervention" hidden="false"><description>Destroyers and Frigates only, and it costs no order. When a friendly ship within 3″ is attacked, rammed, or targeted by torpedoes, a Destroyer or Frigate no more than 10″ from the attacker may thrust into the firing line: it does not move, and the whole attack resolves against it instead, striking whichever facing lies toward the attacker. Once per ship per battle round.</description></rule><rule id="33a73f65-3e56-518c-ba77-3069d137326d" name="Keyword: Wolf Pack" hidden="false"><description>Destroyers of one squadron within 6″ may combine fire on a single target, adding +1 to penetration. Gunnery only, never Torpedo Tubes. Frigates do not have Wolf Pack; they have Screen.</description></rule><rule id="e4b5dc22-981c-5f71-b90b-91982ae54cc8" name="Keyword: Melta Mines" hidden="false"><description>Each Frigate may carry two Melta Mines. No other class may take them. In the Movement step, after the Frigate has moved and instead of shooting, place a mine on a 32mm base in contact with the ship's base — one mine per round, Reload (2), and never within 6″ of an enemy ship. A mine detonates the moment any part of a non-Frigate ship's base passes over it. Every ship within 3″, friend or foe and including the ship that triggered it, immediately suffers one hit at Strength 9, AP 2 with Armourbane, resolved against the facing nearest the mine. Melta Mines bypass Void Shields entirely. Frigates of either fleet pass over mines safely, and aircraft ignore them. Remove the marker once the blast is resolved.</description></rule><rule id="b8a48b19-d4d4-59d1-90ef-86453a7890a3" name="Keyword: Broken Fleet" hidden="false"><description>Once three quarters of a fleet's starting points are lost, it loses the battle at once.</description></rule><rule id="19092359-f987-5e03-a3d6-323e289582af" name="Keyword: Screen" hidden="false"><description>Enemy ships suffer −1 BS when targeting a friendly Capital Ship within 3″ of one or more friendly Frigates. Screen protects only Capital Ships, never the Frigate itself, and multiple instances never stack — the maximum is −1 BS.</description></rule><rule id="818dc409-6d7e-5b02-965b-2228b82851a2" name="Keyword: Scout" hidden="false"><description>A Destroyers may deploy up to 6″ ahead of its owner's normal deployment zone, obeying all other deployment restrictions and squadron coherency.</description></rule><rule id="cfd02a54-b5ba-5f47-9b41-925534ed1aa8" name="Keyword: Squadron" hidden="false"><description>Destroyers and Frigates have the Squadron keyword. Each is taken singly and up to 3 may be grouped into one squadron, which acts as a single unit for movement, shooting and Fleet Orders. Every ship in a squadron counts individually toward the fleet's Line Ship total.</description></rule><rule id="98d45890-ff01-5204-9651-359c5879704e" name="Power Spur" hidden="false"><description>A reinforced ramming prow, carried by the Cruiser, Grand Cruiser and Battleship alone. It is not fired: it resolves as part of a Ram (Section 4a) at Strength equal to this ship's Prow Armour Value, and adds Devastating (3) and Armourbane to that attack. One per ship, and it occupies one Prow mount.</description></rule><rule id="2537130f-c781-5713-8da3-4018cea587be" name="Universal Ship Upgrades" hidden="false"><description>Universal Ship Upgrades are open to every ship below Gloriana class, whatever its Legion, role or loadout. Gloriana-class vessels and anything above them may not buy them. Each may be purchased once per ship, and a ship may take any combination. Every upgrade scales with hull class, because a larger hull gets more out of it: the Cruiser pays the listed cost, and other hulls pay ×0.4 (Destroyer, Destroyer), ×0.6 (Frigate), ×0.8 (Assault Barge), ×1.2 (Grand Cruiser), ×1.4 (Battle Barge) or ×1.6 (Battleship, Emperor Battleship), rounded to the nearest 5 points. Reinforced Magazine Compartments (50 pts): reduce the Damage Control caused by a Magazine Explosion by 1, to a minimum of 0. Enhanced Void Shield Array (75 pts): at the end of each battle round regain 1 lost Void Shield, provided the shields are still active and never above the normal maximum. Autoloaders (100 pts): reduce the Reload value of every weapon and system aboard by 1, to a minimum of Reload (0). Side Armour Reinforcement (75 pts), Engine Refit (100 pts), Phosphex Shells (50 pts) and Veteran Crew (95 pts) scale on the same ladder.</description></rule><rule id="ad0306c1-db2e-5469-84d5-ea7897d575c1" name="Ship Classes" hidden="false"><description>The Imperial hull progression: Destroyer → Frigate → Light Cruiser → Cruiser → Grand Cruiser → Battleship → Emperor Battleship → Gloriana. Assault Barges and Battle Barges are Astartes assault warships and sit outside that progression; the Abyss is its own super-capital category, and the Phalanx its own Void Fortress class. Line Ships are the Destroyer, Frigate, Light Cruiser, Assault Barge and Cruiser. Capital Ships are the Grand Cruiser, Battle Barge, Battleship, Emperor Battleship, Gloriana and Abyss. Void Fortress is the topmost class and the Phalanx alone; it counts as a Capital Ship for every rule that names one, except where its own datasheet says otherwise.</description></rule><rule id="cb287560-cbe3-5b93-bc4a-0b708d177d33" name="Scuttle Ship" hidden="false"><description>Any ship may scuttle itself once reduced to a quarter or less of its starting Hull Points. Round the quarter up, so a 16 HP Gloriana may scuttle at 4 or fewer and a 6 HP Cruiser at 2 or fewer. • When issued: at any point in the ship's own activation. • Effect: the ship is destroyed at once and automatically suffers a Catastrophic Explosion — do not roll the D6 that normally decides it. Resolve the blast for its class as normal (Section 7). • Losses: every Character, Primarch and remaining Crew aboard is lost with her. • Restrictions: the decision cannot be cancelled once declared. A scuttled ship is not a wreck and leaves none behind. A ship destroyed by another ship's blast does not itself scuttle, so no chain of scuttles can occur; it rolls to explode as normal. • A ship that has attempted a Reactor Overload this round may still scuttle, but a reactor already dead-fired confers no further effect.</description></rule><rule id="2d07e688-c8f9-59dd-9e7d-803cb293e10c" name="Characters &amp; Primarchs" hidden="false"><description>One commander per fleet, the highest rank present. He is assigned to a ship when the fleet is built and remains aboard for the whole battle.
• Ranks: Fleet Captain (free, 1 order of each type), Named Character (2), Primarch (3). Ranks never combine, and where a datasheet grants a different number that number replaces the rank's rather than adding to it.
• Assigned aboard: a Character or Primarch may never leave his ship, transfer to another, join a boarding party, ride a drop pod or assault craft, or escape a crippled or scuttled hull. If his ship is destroyed or scuttled he is lost with it, and the fleet nominates a new Flagship at the next Muster.
• Range: abilities work from his ship, and reach other ships only where the ability states a range.
• Command ability: Fleet Captain — Ship's Master; Named Character — Practised Command; Primarch — The Fleet Obeys.
• Demigod of War: a Primarch fights in every boarding action involving his ship, attacking or defending, rolling his own die at +3. He is never a Crew point.
• Primarch's Retinue: a fleet led by a Primarch may include one further named Character of the same Legion aboard any Capital Ship. He adds no Fleet Orders, no Command range and no command ability; only his other abilities apply.
• Minimum game size: a Primarch may be fielded only at 2,000 points or more.</description></rule><rule id="03faafcc-fd26-5480-a298-432218ff599d" name="Keyword: Vortex Torpedo" hidden="false"><description>A Vortex Torpedo occupies 2 Prow mounts and may be mounted nowhere else. There is no limit beyond the mounts it consumes — a hull with 4 Prow mounts may carry two. Strength 12, AP D, 60″, One Shot, Devastating (3), Volatile. Like any torpedo it bypasses Void Shields entirely, resolving against the hull facing struck; unlike a Nova Cannon it is not stopped by a live envelope.</description></rule></sharedRules></catalogue>